Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790323199999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["Strongest counterargument: the 2850 high is a single-bar spike (bar 117) with a 74.39-point upper tail, and bars 118-120 give no follow-through above it; a failed breakout would rotate price back into the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Upside spike attempts inside this window have repeatedly failed: 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range, so an overshoot above a range top is a recurring pattern here.", "Bar 119 closes at 2684.16, back below the 2771 prior swing high, so the break above that swing high is not yet accepted.", "Near-term momentum has turned down: bars 118 and 119 are the first two consecutive lower closes since bar 113, and bar 119 closes in the lower quarter of its range.", "Bars 87-113 (27 of the last 34 bars before the breakout) traded two-sided inside 2357.18-2680, so an alternative read is a broad trading range with only a marginal upside overshoot, i.e., phase more channel/range than a fresh spike.", "Bars 115 and 116 barely advance (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) between the two strong bars, and the leg from bar 106 to 2850 contains overlapping pullbacks, which is channel rather than pure spike behavior."], "evidence_for": ["The 120-bar window shows an unbroken sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42, 1512.91, 1597.72, 1803.74, 2357.18, 2633.31) and higher swing highs (1944.39, 2771, 2850), which is the core of the bull-trend classification.", "Bar 84 is a large bull trend bar closing at the top of its range with follow-through to 2771 (bars 85-86), showing acceptance above the 1803.74-1974.46 range rather than a one-bar overshoot.", "The compressed final range (bars 73-83 inside 1863.68-1937.76) is a tight-range/bull-flag structure that resolved upward, consistent with trend continuation rather than a top.", "The latest leg (bars 114, 117) closes above both the 2680 range top and the 2771 prior swing high, so the current structure is a breakout to a new high, not a rotation inside the 2357.18-2680 range.", "Bar 120 holds above the 2680 range top and closes above its open (2686.59 versus 2684.16), so no bear breakout or acceptance back inside the range has occurred.", "The bearish bars after the high are small relative to the preceding bull bars (bar 119 range 145.44 versus bar 117 range 208.31), and no bear trend bar has follow-through."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars; window low 1368.42 (bar 10, open_time 1780704000000) and window high 2850 (bar 117, open_time 1789948800000); first close 2009.45 versus last close 2686.59.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to 1568.55, taking price to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 and leaves a 200.13-point lower tail (low 1368.42 versus close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-35 form a two-sided range with repeated highs at 1725.85 (bar 18) and 1845.09 (bar 19) and repeated lows at 1512.91 (bar 30) and 1551.60 (bar 34); bull and bear reversal bars alternate.", "Bars 36-49 rise on two wide bull trend bars (bar 36: 1608.68 to 1701.02; bar 48: 1775.60 to 1889.93, high 1891.66), reaching the 1944.39 high at bar 49.", "Bars 50-83 form a long, tight range: high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51); bars 73-83 overlap inside 1863.68-1937.76.", "Bar 84 (open_time 1787097600000) is a large bull trend bar, 1916.51 to 2252.16, closing 96% of its 377.29 range, the widest bar in the window, above the 1974.46 range top.", "Bars 87-113 hold a broad range: low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike highs at 2557.46 (bar 92), 2680 (bar 107) and 2609.02 (bar 110) were each closed back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 break upward: bar 114 closes 2612.02 (85% of its 206.65 range), bar 115 taps 2700, bar 117 reaches a new window high 2850 and closes 2775.61 with a 74.39-point upper tail.", "Bars 118-120 pull back: bar 119 is a bear bar closing 2684.16 in the lower quarter of its 145.44 range; bar 120 is a small bull bar (open 2684.16, close 2686.59) with low 2633.31, holding above the 2680 range top.", "Higher swing lows: 1368.42 (bar 10), 1512.91 (bar 30), 1597.72 (bar 36), 1803.74 (bar 51), 2357.18 (bar 98), 2633.31 (bar 120). Higher swing highs: 1944.39 (bar 49), 2771 (bar 86), 2850 (bar 117)."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Sell climax ending the window's down leg: bars 6-10 post five consecutive lower closes from 2006.17 to the window low 1368.42; bar 10 closes 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail.", "end_time_ms": 1780703999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2006.17"}, {"description": "Post-sell-off two-sided range (bars 11-35): repeated tests of the 1512.91-1551.60 low area and the 1725.85-1845.09 high area, with most closes between 1550 and 1730.", "end_time_ms": 1782950399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Long, tight range (bars 50-83): high 1974.46 (bar 61), low 1803.74 (bar 51), compressing into 1863.68-1937.76 for bars 73-83 immediately before the bar 84 breakout.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull breakout and spike (bars 84-86): bar 84 runs 1916.51 to 2252.16 and closes near its high, above the 1974.46 range top; follow-through carries to the spike high 2771 at bar 86.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Broad post-spike range (bars 87-113): low 2357.18 (bar 98), high 2680 (bar 107); spike attempts at 2557.46, 2680 and 2609.02 all closed back inside.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Current bull leg (bars 114-117): two strong bull trend bars plus an overlapping pair break above the 2680 range top and the 2771 swing high to a new window high 2850; bars 118-120 pull back to 2633.31, still above 2680.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2850, or a bar closing in the upper third of its range above 2775.61, would confirm the breakout-spike read and favor trend continuation.", "Two consecutive closes below 2633.31 (bar 120 low) would indicate a failed breakout and rotation back into the 2357.18-2680 range, moving phase toward range.", "A strong bear trend bar closing below 2357.18 (bar 98 low) would end the sequence of higher swing lows and shift the regime read to trading-range or transition-unclear.", "Continued overlapping bars and closes inside 2633.31-2786.81 without reaching 2850 again would raise the odds that the last leg is a channel within a broad top, changing phase to channel and lowering always-in relevance.", "A pullback that holds above the 2436.87-2514.13 breakout area and then produces a close above 2786.81 would keep the bull-trend read while confirming the pullback as a buy-the-close-style continuation leg of the channel."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790308799999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The 2850.00 bar closed 2723.15 in the lower third of its 2658.06-2850.00 range - a weak close at a new extreme - and the following high 2804.59 is a lower high.", "The latest swing is down then sideways, not up: 2850.00 to 2633.31 (216.69 points) with the 2716.01-2804.59 range broken at 1790164800000.", "2700.00 has capped price repeatedly: exact highs at 1789804800000 and 1789948800000, then four tests capping at 2695.84/2698.06/2699.39/2699.53 with no close above, and the last bar closed 2677.28.", "The pullback is deeper than any inside the rally - about 44% of the 2358.62-2850.00 leg versus earlier pullbacks of roughly 60-120 points (e.g., 2643.52 down to 2568.16).", "Since 1790179200000 bars overlap heavily with no more than two consecutive same-direction closes, so the recent tape is two-sided rather than a trend."], "evidence_for": ["Swing structure over the window is up: the 2411.04 low of 1789041600000 was undercut at 2358.62, and every major swing low afterwards is higher (2370.54, then 2568.16, then 2633.31).", "Two bull accelerations carry closes into the upper half of their bars: 1789732800000 (2578.60 within 2495.82-2585.50) and 1789747200000 (2636.28 within 2578.44-2643.52), plus 1789977600000 closing 2723.15 after opening 2658.81.", "The bear spike at 1790164800000 (close 2659.00) was immediately reversed by 1790179200000 (close 2676.47), a failed break below 2716.01 with no bear follow-through bar.", "The last 9 bars have rising lows and 8 of 9 closes above the range midpoint, a marginal bull always-in inside the range.", "The 2633.31 pullback low holds above the 2568.16-2570.00 support shelf, and price remains about 65% up the 2358.62-2850.00 leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars, 1788580800000 through 1790294400000; first close 2456.52, last close 2677.28 (net +220.76).", "Window low 2358.62 at 1789488000000; window high 2850.00 at 1789977600000, 34 bars later; both extremes sit in the second half of the window.", "Bull bar at 1789128000000 opened 2457.12, high 2680.00, low 2444.19, close 2555.52 - a very large bar that engulfed several prior bars.", "Bear bars at 1789473600000 (low 2390.73, close 2423.29) and 1789488000000 (low 2358.62, close 2412.95) ended in a five-bar base with lows 2381.00/2370.54 before the rally.", "The 2850.00 bar (1789977600000) closed 2723.15, about 34% of its 2658.06-2850.00 range (long upper tail); the next high, 2804.59 at 1790020800000, is a lower high.", "After 2850.00 the tape is two-sided: 11 bars between 2716.01 and 2804.59, then the bar at 1790164800000 (low 2648.49, close 2659.00) closed below 2716.01 with no bear follow-through.", "Last 9 bars (1790179200000-1790294400000) span 2633.31-2699.53 with ranges of roughly 20-60 points; 8 of 9 closes are above the 2666.42 midpoint and lows rise 2633.31, 2640.00, 2660.49, 2673.88.", "Exact 2700.00 highs at 1789804800000 and 1789948800000; later highs stop at 2695.84, 2698.06, 2699.39 (1790265600000) and 2699.53 (1790294400000), and the last bar closed 2677.28 back below 2700.", "The 2850.00 to 2633.31 pullback is 216.69 points, about a 44% retracement of the 2358.62-2850.00 rally; the last close is about 65% up that leg."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Two-sided early-window range: about 30 overlapping bars capped by the 2528.80 high (1788739200000) and floored near 2441.33 (1788868800000); repeated pushes into 2510-2529 failed, and the bar at 1789041600000 broke below the floor to 2411.04.", "end_time_ms": 1789041599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2441.33", "start_time_ms": 1788580800000, "upper_boundary": "2528.80"}, {"description": "Bear spike from the 2609.02 high (1789416000000) to the window low 2358.62 (1789488000000): large bear bars at 1789473600000 (low 2390.73, close 2423.29) and 1789488000000 (low 2358.62, close 2412.95) broke the earlier 2411.04 low, then price based with lows 2381.00/2370.54.", "end_time_ms": 1789487999999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789416000000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 2358.62 low (1789488000000) to the 2850.00 high (1789977600000) in two accelerations: bull bars at 1789732800000 (close 2578.60) and 1789747200000 (close 2636.28), then 1789977600000 (high 2850.00) and 1789992000000 (close 2754.31). Intervening pullbacks were shallow and overlapping (2568.16 at 1789891200000; 2716.01 at 1790049600000).", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850.00"}, {"description": "Post-spike two-sided range of 11 bars between 2804.59 (1790020800000) and 2716.01 (1790049600000), entirely below the 2850.00 high; the bar at 1790164800000 (close 2659.00) closed below 2716.01 and ended the range downward.", "end_time_ms": 1790179199999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2716.01", "start_time_ms": 1790006400000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Possible top shape, not a confirmed reversal: higher high 2850.00 with a weak close (2723.15) at 1789977600000, a lower high 2804.59 at 1790020800000, then a break below 2716.01 at 1790164800000; that break got no follow-through because 1790179200000 closed back up at 2676.47 and the next 8 bars held above 2633.31.", "end_time_ms": 1790308799999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850.00"}, {"description": "Current 9-bar range 2633.31 (1790236800000) to 2699.53 (1790294400000): small overlapping bars (about 20-60 points of range), 8 of 9 closes in the upper half, rising lows, and repeated stops just under the exact 2700.00 highs printed at 1789804800000 and 1789948800000.", "end_time_ms": 1790308799999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790179200000, "upper_boundary": "2699.53"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resumption: a close above 2700.00 and t